WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.780
Hello, Office Ladies family.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.640
Before we get started with today's episode, we have some sad news to share.

3
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:06.460
We do.

4
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:11.240
Our hearts are broken, and our dear Phil Shea has passed away.

5
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:18.380
We just wanted to share that news with you because he was a part of our Office family.

6
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.820
He was a part of our Office Ladies family.

7
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.800
I was just in touch with Phil recently.

8
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.040
We were trading some text messages about Pam's chore wheel.

9
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:37.100
And something I can tell you is just how much he loved sharing his passion, his work with everyone.

10
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:43.800
And he loved that you all took such an interest in all of his props and all of his work.

11
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.360
And it was his pride and joy, and we're so happy that we got to share it with you.

12
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.100
Yes.

13
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.300
When I ran into him a few months ago, he told me how much it meant to him that

14
00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:01.320
people on Office Ladies knew his name, knew what he did.

15
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.880
So thank you for being part of our Office family,

16
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.200
and we will miss Phil very much.

17
00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.100
We will.

18
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.260
We love you, Phil.

19
00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:09.980
Love you.

20
00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:15.710
I'm Jenna Fisher.

21
00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:17.010
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

22
00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.290
We were on The Office together.

23
00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:19.550
And we're best friends.

24
00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:23.350
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch Podcast just for you.

25
00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:28.070
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories

26
00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.350
that only two people who were there can tell you.

27
00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.490
We're The Office Ladies.

28
00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:38.430
Oh, you guys, guess what I was just doing?

29
00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.970
As our theme song comes on, we listen to it

30
00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.030
every time we record.

31
00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.070
Is that dorky?

32
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.270
It is dorky, but it gets me in the mood.

33
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:45.830
Me too.

34
00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:49.550
And it makes me excited to hop on here and talk about The Office.

35
00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:50.790
So we listened

36
00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.110
to our theme song with you guys.

37
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.330
And this morning, I decided to dance.

38
00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:56.190
I did a little dance.

39
00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:56.830
She did?

40
00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:57.130
Uh-huh.

41
00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:58.370
We do that sometimes.

42
00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:06.450
Yeah, I did a little shimmy.

43
00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:07.090
You did.

44
00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.210
You shimmied the ladies.

45
00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.710
I shimmied the ladies today.

46
00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.930
And I'm glad we did it.

47
00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:13.390
Yeah.

48
00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:15.990
Because, oh boy.

49
00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.030
Uh-oh.

50
00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:19.730
That's a big sigh.

51
00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.650
Today, we're completing season eight.

52
00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.650
Yeah, this is it.

53
00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.550
This is the last episode of season eight.

54
00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.470
It's season eight, episode 24.

55
00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.610
It's called Free Family Portrait Studio.

56
00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.250
It was written

57
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.250
by BJ Novak and directed by BJ Novak.

58
00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.850
He was wearing a lot of hats.

59
00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:47.950
On this last week of 24 episodes, poor BJ, he must have been so tired.

60
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.050
I mean, we were

61
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.190
all tired, but I think BJ must have been super tired.

62
00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.650
This was also my birthday week.

63
00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:55.570
Oh, yeah.

64
00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.330
My birthday happened in this week.

65
00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.630
I bet you were tired on your birthday.

66
00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:02.350
I was tired on my birthday.

67
00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:07.030
Oh, but we did the cutest thing for my birthday during this

68
00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:07.290
week.

69
00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:10.150
We were filming over March 7th, which is my birthday.

70
00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.010
And you guys got me a cake, which was really, really sweet.

71
00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:14.330
Oh, yeah.

72
00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:20.290
And Lee brought my son up to set for the cake and the singing, which was so adorable.

73
00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:23.710
And we were doing talking heads at that time.

74
00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.830
That's what we were set up to do.

75
00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.490
And so we

76
00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:30.050
put my son in the talking head chair.

77
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:30.890
That's adorable.

78
00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.590
And they filmed a little bit of him.

79
00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:33.510
Oh.

80
00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:34.350
I know.

81
00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:39.070
And I just wrote to Dave Rogers and asked him if there was any way that he

82
00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.290
could find that footage.

83
00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.690
Because that memory came back to me when I was watching this episode.

84
00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.030
So he's going to look for it.

85
00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:46.450
Somebody has that footage.

86
00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:50.870
And somebody at NBC also has when Creed and Ed sang Angela's

87
00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:51.530
baby to me.

88
00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:53.390
We want these things.

89
00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:54.310
Someone at NBC.

90
00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.190
I know.

91
00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.610
Get it to us.

92
00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.870
I just sounded so Southern.

93
00:03:58.970 --> 00:03:59.490
You did.

94
00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.690
Get it to us.

95
00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:01.530
Dang it.

96
00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.070
Are you ready for a summary?

97
00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:04.350
I am.

98
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.130
Last summary of season eight.

99
00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.850
Are we going to do this the whole episode?

100
00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:10.150
I'm going to do it the whole season nine.

101
00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.110
So just get ready.

102
00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:11.570
Oh, no.

103
00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.030
Okay.

104
00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:13.290
Here's your summary.

105
00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:20.410
In an effort to prove his paternity once and for all, Dwight sets up a portrait studio in

106
00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:22.350
the office for all of the employees.

107
00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:26.330
He's hoping to steal some of baby Philip's DNA for

108
00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:26.870
testing.

109
00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:32.690
Andy pretends to be down and out, but he has a secret plan to become manager again thanks

110
00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:33.670
to David Wallace.

111
00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.810
I loved when Nellie calls him like a drunken chimney sweep.

112
00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.030
Such a good description.

113
00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:46.350
Robert California reveals his true identity after Joe Bennett dissolves Saber, and Daryl

114
00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.270
makes his intentions clear with Val.

115
00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:49.710
There's a lot happening.

116
00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:50.270
Yeah.

117
00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:54.370
I have lots to say about their impromptu photo shoot.

118
00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:55.810
We'll get to it.

119
00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:58.690
Oh, we got a lot of mail about it, Ange.

120
00:04:58.710 --> 00:04:59.090
Uh-huh.

121
00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:00.050
Yeah.

122
00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:05.250
Are you ready for the last Fast Fact number one of season eight?

123
00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.250
I mean, I guess so.

124
00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.270
Here it is.

125
00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:14.010
Like we said, this was our season eight finale, and it marked a number of goodbyes.

126
00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:17.750
We mentioned that BJ Novak wrote and directed this episode.

127
00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:20.490
This was his last episode as

128
00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.990
a writer on The Office.

129
00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.670
He'd been with us since the very beginning.

130
00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.750
This was also Mindy

131
00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.510
Kaling's last episode as a writer.

132
00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.310
She left to start her own show, The Mindy Project.

133
00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:36.490
I remember just at the time being like, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

134
00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:37.530
You guys can't go.

135
00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:43.130
It felt like we were losing our core team that built and defined the whole show.

136
00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.050
I call them the originals.

137
00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.090
The OGs.

138
00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:46.470
Mm-hmm.

139
00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:46.870
Mm-hmm.

140
00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:47.870
That's what kids say.

141
00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:48.690
They say the OG.

142
00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.830
Oh, not the originals.

143
00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:58.810
So, you know, Mindy and BJ are going to appear as actors a couple times in season nine, but this

144
00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.710
ended their time as writers and regulars on the show.

145
00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.790
And then Paul Lieberstein was also

146
00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:08.690
stepping down as showrunner after this season.

147
00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:14.510
There was a lot of discussion about who might step into the showrunner position.

148
00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.950
I dare say there was hubbub, lady.

149
00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.090
Oh, I think that is accurate.

150
00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:19.650
Yes.

151
00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:20.290
Hubbub.

152
00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.750
Hubbub about the originals.

153
00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:23.590
Yes.

154
00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:24.390
Leaving.

155
00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:32.990
Well, I remember John and I went over to BJ's trailer and we asked him to please consider

156
00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.650
taking the showrunner position for season nine.

157
00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.290
We told him nobody else knew the show as well

158
00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.030
as he did.

159
00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:44.370
We were very, what would you call it, passionate.

160
00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:45.770
Yes.

161
00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:47.610
You guys wanted him to stay.

162
00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.790
And he said no.

163
00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:50.890
He said no.

164
00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:51.290
Yeah.

165
00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:55.070
I could tell he was really touched, but he said he felt really burnt out.

166
00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.170
He needed to move on.

167
00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.930
Well, I can understand that.

168
00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:58.550
I know.

169
00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:02.810
And when you're writing and creating, you can't be in a space where you're burnt out.

170
00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:03.290
No.

171
00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:04.930
Another goodbye?

172
00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.170
James Spader.

173
00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:07.350
Yes.

174
00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:08.590
He was moving on.

175
00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:11.890
You know, he'd really just agreed to do the one season.

176
00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:12.590
Right.

177
00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:15.830
So we were saying goodbye to him after this episode.

178
00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:18.190
We also say goodbye to Saber.

179
00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:19.830
Goodbye, Saber.

180
00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:20.230
Yeah.

181
00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.330
Saber's no more.

182
00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.170
Sabre.

183
00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.290
So we had a lot of goodbyes.

184
00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:24.710
Mm-hmm.

185
00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:27.270
But we also had a lot of, oh, hellos.

186
00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.370
Oh, okay.

187
00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.090
Hello.

188
00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:30.030
Oh, hello.

189
00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.070
Hello again, Senator Lipton.

190
00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:32.630
Yes.

191
00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.030
Hey there, David Wallace.

192
00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:34.910
Yes.

193
00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:37.950
Oh, hi, Jerry Miner is Val's boyfriend, Brandon.

194
00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:40.430
Hi there, warehouse fellas.

195
00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:41.370
Now, is this-

196
00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:41.420
Hiday.

